-------------------------------------------------------------------------
A. Introduction
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

This example shows how to implement a basic functioning UVM testbench using UART
Verification IP. A quickstart navigation guide can be found at:
    
HTML Quickstart is available @ $DESIGNWARE_HOME/vip/svt/uart_svt/latest/examples/sverilog/tb_uart_svt_uvm_basic_sys/doc/tb_uart_svt_uvm_basic_sys/index_basic.html
    
The example consists of the following:

- A top-level testbench in SystemVerilog
- A hdl_interconnect representing the UART in the testbench and DTE UART 
  and DCE UART interfaces are connected to hdl_interconnect
- UVM verification environment
- UART DTE and DCE slave agents are instantiated in the UVM verification environment
- Four test files illustrating 
  i.   Basic test with default sequence
  ii.  Directed test with directed sequences
  iii. Random test with random sequence
  iv.  Reconfig test with reconfig sequence

The UVM Synopsys Discovery UART VIP agents are connected in the following manner:

                                     (UART Env)
    ==================================================================================
  ||     (UART DTE Agent)                                        (UART DCE Agent)     ||
  ||   ---------------------                                    -------------------   ||
  ||  |  ------    -------  |                                  |  -----   -------  |  ||
  ||  | | DTE  |  |Monitor| |        ------------------        | | DCE | |Monitor| |  ||
  ||  |  ------    -------  |<=====>| hdl_interconnect |<=====>|  -----   -------  |  ||
  ||  |    *Active Mode*    |        ------------------        |   *Active Mode*   |  ||
  ||   \___________________/                                    \_________________/   ||
  ||                                                                                  ||
    ==================================================================================


In the remainder of this description, <design_dir> refers to the directory where
the example was installed using script dw_vip_setup. The example source files
would then exist at two locations:

- "$DESIGNWARE_HOME/vip/svt/uart_svt/latest/examples/sverilog/tb_uart_svt_uvm_basic_sys" 
- "<design_dir>/examples/sverilog/uart_svt/tb_uart_svt_uvm_basic_sys" 

Note :- the quickstart guide is _only_ available at
$DESIGNWARE_HOME/vip/svt/uart_svt/latest/examples/sverilog/tb_uart_svt_uvm_basic_sys/doc/tb_uart_svt_uvm_basic_sys/index_basic.html
The quickstart is not installed in <design_dir>. Unless otherwise noted, the files
described below are also found in <design_dir>.  

Complete class reference HTML documentation of UART UVM Verification 
IP is available at:
  
$DESIGNWARE_HOME/vip/svt/uart_svt/latest/doc/uart_svt_uvm_class_reference/html/index.html
Note: Class reference has UVM 1.1d Base Class Library only.

User guide, getting started and release notes pdf's are present under :
$DESIGNWARE_HOME/vip/svt/uart_svt/latest/doc/uart_svt_uvm_user_guide.pdf
$DESIGNWARE_HOME/vip/svt/uart_svt/latest/doc/uart_svt_uvm_getting_started.pdf
$DESIGNWARE_HOME/vip/svt/uart_svt/latest/doc/uart_svt_release_notes.pdf

------------------------------------------------------------------------
B. Running the Example Testbench
------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Install the example using the following command line:

   % cd <location where example is to be installed>
   % mkdir design_dir <provide any name of your choice>
   % $DESIGNWARE_HOME/bin/dw_vip_setup -path ./design_dir  -e uart_svt/tb_uart_svt_uvm_basic_sys -svtb 

2. Use either one of the following to run the testbench:

   a) Use the Makefile:

      Four tests are provided in the "tests" directory.
      The tests are: 
      1. ts.base_test.sv 
      2. ts.directed_test.sv 
      3. ts.random_test.sv 
      4. ts.reconfig_test.sv 

      For example, to run test ts.directed_test.sv, do following:
      
      gmake USE_SIMULATOR=vcsvlog directed_test WAVES=1

      Invoke "gmake help" to show more options.
   
   b) Use the sim script:

     For example, to run test ts.random_test.sv, do following:

     ./run_uart_svt_uvm_basic_sys -w random_test vcsvlog-svlog 

      Invoke "./run_uart_svt_uvm_basic_sys -help" to show more options.


