-------------------------------------------------------------------------
D. SystemVerilog Testbench Description
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

The  top-level testbench is written in SystemVerilog. The UART interfaces 
are represented as instances of 'interface' objects. The hdl_interconnect 
is represented as a UART model with 'interface' connections as its ports.
The UVM verification environment is represented as an uart_basic_env instance.
The test file is created as a class which extends uart_base_test.

The file containing the top-level testbench in the example is "top.sv".  
This file which encapsulates individual tests is "top_test.sv".

The UART model used in the example is defined as a hdl_interconnect, within a SystemVerilog
wrapper. The intent is to demonstrate how a legacy core may be integrated into
the SystemVerilog testbench. The example UART model has DTE and DCE UART interfaces. 


The SystemVerilog wrapper for the UART model defines a module that takes 'interface'
references as its port connections. The SystemVerilog wrapper instantiates
the Verilog UART bus model, and connects UART DTE and DCE interfaces to the UART model.

The example UART bus model is found in the file "hdl_interconnect.v". The example wrapper
is found in the file "uart_svt_interconnect_sv_wrapper.sv".

The entire UVM test environment is encapsulated in uart_basic_env.sv, which is
instantiated in the UVM tests.  The tests gets included in 'top.sv',
which eventually triggers the specific test by the use of run_test().

-------------------------------------------------------------------------
E. UVM Verification Environment Description
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

A complete description of the UVM environment (ENV) is beyond the scope of this
README. Please refer to the UVM manual for details of a UVM environment.

Following is a summary of the files used by the ENV:

  - uart_svt_interconnect_sv_wrapper.sv.  A SystemVerilog module that wraps the
    verilog RTL Interconnect.  This will be instantiated in the top-level SystemVerilog
    file.
  
  - uart_basic_env.sv
    This file serves as environment class.  The top-level environment is
    implemented by extending uvm_env base class.  This class instantiates the
    UART DTE and DCE agents and a virtual sequencer.

  - cust_svt_uart_agent_configuration.sv
    This file extends agent configuration (svt_uart_agent_configuration).
    All the necessary configuration parameters are set up for the environment
    in this class.

  - cust_svt_uart_transaction.sv
    This file extends the transaction (svt_uart_transaction).
    Customized constraints are defined by this class.

  - uart_simple_reset_sequence.sv
    This file shows a virtual sequence that generates a simple sequence
    to drive the reset pins.  This sequence is registered with the TB
    virtual sequencer as the default sequence for the reset phase.

  - uart_default_virtual_sequence.sv
    This file implements a virtual sequence executes an
    uart_default_sequence on DTE and DCE agent sequencer.  This sequence is registered with the 
    UART ENV virtual sequencer as the default sequence for the main
    phase.

  - uart_null_virtual_sequence.sv
    This file implements a virtual sequence with an empty body method.  This
    sequence can be used by extended tests to disable the default sequence.

  - uart_random_sequence.sv
    This file shows a sequence (extending from uvm_sequence)
    that generates constrained random svt_uart_transaction.  This is the
    default sequence that set up by the base test.

  - uart_directed_sequence.sv
    This file shows a sequence (extending from uvm_sequence)
    that generates a series of directed svt_uart_transaction.

  - uart_default_sequence.sv
    This file shows a sequence (extending from uvm_sequence)
    that generates a default random svt_uart_transaction.

